      controller through a mock web request harness; a derived report must not manufacture one;
    no failure, error or skipped child element appears, because this class carries no ignore annotation
      and no outcome was observed for it.
  This class boots a SPRING WEB CONTEXT, so its baseline outcome is environment dependent and CANNOT be
  inferred from the source. The mechanism is concrete rather than theoretical. The context is assembled
  from two locations and only one of them lives in this module: the in module location declares a single
  bean, an exception handler resolver, which the class injects and hands to the mock web request harness
  it builds in its fixture method; the other location is not present in this module at all and reaches
  the test only as a classpath resource out of a different module's installed artifact. Whether that
  context resolves therefore depends on the reactor having built and installed that other module, which
  is a property of the run and not of the file. Reading the source can establish which test methods
  existed; it cannot establish whether they passed.
  Validation of this migration asserts on produced artifacts and on captured output, never on a process
  exit status alone. Archiving the report rather than a pass or fail claim about a run is that principle
